/div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's not the &quot;Babes&quot; or &quot;Hunks&quot; threads...because they were...what exactly? Inappropriate for some reason? I forget.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between talking about sex and basking in sexualisation. I think this thread will be just fine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T15:18:36-08:00","id":52797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=50033#post50033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I direct posters to the &quot;no threadcrapping&quot; rule (#2). Forum rules are linked in my sig.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Its not the thread I'm crapping on, boyo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T15:28:48-08:00","id":52802,"title":"","content":"Before I start dissecting my own sexual hangups, I'll give some background information.<br /> A few people here already know that I'm a bisexual guy in my mid-20s, with more than a few social and psychiatric issues. The psychiatric part is just background here, unless I get sidetracked at a later point in this post. It happens.<br /> Anyway, I've known I was attracted to both genders from an early age. Due to my usual shyness and tendency to spend my time reading or watching cartoons quietly by myself, for many years that only meant my schoolyard crushes had VARIETY. I didn't talk to many people. My parents worked alot and there was a large amount of 'alone time', and one can't bring up a subject without someone to talk to.<br /> It wasn't until about age ten that it became clear that my father was extremely homophobic. My mother had a few friends from work who were gay, and he made it clear that he disapproved of my mom socializing with them. When I disappointed him in some fashion, I was often called emasculating names. I'm mentioning this on the off-chance that it's somehow related to my main subject.<br /> So, here it is. The Sex part.<br /> If you don't want to see frank, personal information about my sexual preferences !Stop Reading Now!<br /> <br /> I 've always enjoyed being penetrated during sex or masturbation. This has never been an issue for me emotionally, despite certain bad experiences. I've never actually been intimate with a man (though I have had a short-lived romantic relationship with one that ended before we could become intimate), despite my orientation, so this has been with women I've dated and by myself thus far.<br /> I find the thought of being penetrated by a man highly arousing, and would have no issue (I think) performing oral sex on a male partner. My issue is, the thought of penetrating someone else, orally or otherwise, is a HUGE turnoff for me. I really dislike the thought of someone coming into contact with my penis. It's led to quite a few embarrassing situations, but again, only with women thus far. It's hard to describe the look of sheer confusion and disbelief on a woman's face (a woman you were only moments before groping and kissing passionately) when you tell her you don't like to get &quot;touched there&quot;.<br /> I'm going to go on a tangent for a moment, but it'll get back to my previous point. I don't enjoy masturbating. I do it, but I'm often disgusted with my own body as I do. After orgasm, I often feel depressed and thoughts tend to linger about how 'wrong' and pathetic I feel the act to be. I don't find the idea of other people masturbating repellent. Quite the opposite, in fact. I have no idea why this is. I've also done some crossdressing in the past. I'll go out on a limb and say that this is just because ladies underwear make me feel sexier and more confident.Ok, back to my main ...point?<br /> If, by this point, you're wondering whether I have a genuine dislike for my genitals, the answer is yes. I don't like the way they look or feel. I've been reading a few posts by other forumites lately about their issue with gender and sexuality, but I don't know if I can say that I'm feeling something similar. I don't think I feel especially feminine (whatever that means, really). I also can't quite define femininity or masculinity for myself, though. I'm told that I'm a lot like my mom, and the similarities in our mannerisms are actually more pronounced than those of my sister and our mom. The same goes for my aunt and grandmother.<br /> I used to think my interests decidedly masculine, but on further reflection, they're really not. I collect knives (but then, so does Angelina Jolie) and I play RPGs (gender neutral). My other interests are horror, comics, fantasy and video games. Sounds like the interests of half the nerds and hobbyists I've ever known, of either gender. I like a few sports (two, not counting martial arts), but that means absolutely nothing. I have, on more than a few occasions wished I had a female body for various reasons. I almost feel silly asking this after letting that out of my head for the first time and seeing it all in black and white, but, could this just be an issue with self esteem or poor self image? I don't want to jump to conclusions, and I'm not too sure what the hell I'm trying to say here.....<br /> <br /> Oh, on a lighter, less confusing note:<br /> <br /> \u200bCan anyone tell me just how painful nipple-piercings are to get? I suspect my sister is lying to me when she says they feel like &quot;only a strong pinch&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 01-18-2014, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T15:38:43-08:00","id":52808,"title":"","content":"Don't mind me...I am just a sadomasochistic switch with no libido. As for nipple piercing, can't tell you anything. I think they dull the area and you are done. Elisabeth got her Marilyn Monroe piercing with no problem. Warning though...you will became super-sensitive if stimulated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:38:46-08:00","id":53467,"title":"","content":"Azrael: I will probably have things to say about the rest of your post, when I have more time, but on the subject of nipple piercings....<br /> <br /> It depends strongly on the skill of your piercer (a shaky, unsure hand can cause a lot of extra pain. A piercer who knows exactly what they need to do and then does it in one quick motion can be nearly painless by comparison) and on your anatomy. People with less breast tissue tend to feel it more acutely, but in any case the pain is over in a moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T01:54:11-08:00","id":53826,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Gabby. I've been on the fence about piercings. I'll keep that info in mind.<br /> <br /> As for the other part, I can't even fathom what sort of response ANYONE could really have for my mass of confused musings. so no worries.<br /> <br /> \u200bOh, a thing I noticed:<br /> I'm not sure if it's because I'm fresh from a breakup or just noticing new feelings, but I've been finding myself examining a few of my &quot;platonic&quot; relationships recently. Rebound mentality might be at play here, so I'll remain skeptical of myself for the time being. I've recognised that, in the past, I've relied too strongly on my relationships to define me, or to make me feel stable and safe. I don't know... maybe that insecurity is why I seek attachment at all.<br /> <br /> I keep trying to talk to my ex. I don't know if I should or not. It's a lot like talking to someone you just drunkenly threw up on at a party. Just awkward sentences and then one of you excuses themself, either to shake of the experience, cry or clean up. Part of me wishes I had broken up with her. Not in a mean &quot;Fuck me? NOPE, FUCK YOU!&quot; way, but so I could have saved myself the time. I've wasted a total of 8 years in a row on fruitless mindfuck long-distance relationships and my life shows the fallout. I have zero attachment to the world outside my house. In a normal relationship, that kind of ignoring the world outside your relationship comes with a lot of embraces, romantic kisses and general physical affection. Meanwhile, I haven't so much as kissed someone since 2005. I wasted so many years on chasing smoke and mirrors.<br /> <br /> Depression is doing weird things to my libido and my usual avenues for arousal and release. Violent, non-sexual (if sexualized) imagery creeping in again. It happens sometimes, with varying frequency, and it makes feel feel like a freak afterward. Therapy topic or kink? I have no clue.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 01-20-2014, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T08:52:55-08:00","id":54692,"title":"","content":"Heya! First to answer Azreal on the Nipple Rings point. I am rather thin, with absolutely no breast tissue and minimal pectoral muscles. My nipple ring was fine getting done, overall, but the residual pain and discomfort lasted much longer than for my other piercings. It was the most uncomfortable piercing I've had done so far, and I have an industrial, a tragus, 4 lobe piercings, 1 nipple, navel and a Prince Albert (which, contrary to what one would expect, was the least painful piercing I got, both immediately and in the long term...plus its ancillary benefits are FANTASTIC!!).<br /> <br /> So yes.<br /> <br /> Also, in terms of your issues with your genitalia and such, since you seem to have body issues, have you considered going to a therapist and speaking about them? I have a number of friends who have had body issues in a similar vein. Some have ended up shifting genders, and some have gotten over their issues, but therapy has helped them overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T10:29:07-08:00","id":54749,"title":"","content":"Yeah, on reading the rest of what you've written, Azrael, it definitely doesn't sound <i>unlike</i> gender dysphoria. I would second widdershawns' suggestion of therapy, and I would look specifically for a trans or trans-friendly therapist (not because you necessarily <i>are</i>, but because they're the most likely to be versed in these issues). I would also start looking for groups of trans folk online, to talk about how they felt about things and see how much of it jives with your own experience. <br /> <br /> I dunno. Gender and sex are a hell of a thing, and I don't think there are solid answers so much as...what changes are going to make you happier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T07:29:49-08:00","id":65678,"title":"","content":"I'm going to be seeing a therapist soon, and this is just another thing I need to be honest about as the therapeutic process goes on, regardless of where it leads me. I honestly can't say what would make me feel the most comfortable or happy. I have a lot of answers to find for myself.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.rottenecards.com/ecards/Rottenecards_75941188_dsb5fd998f.