t's as unfamiliar a term to some of you as it was to me. So I figured we could have some fun with it: guess what sex act &quot;paizuri&quot; denotes. (To yourself, I mean. I won't ask you to type out obscene descriptions here.) Just so you're not flying totally blind, here's a few hints:<br /> <br /> * You have very likely heard of this sex act, and may well have performed it.<br /> * Every English term for it (as far as I know) is rather crude.<br /> * It is significantly more pleasurable for one partner than the other.<br /> <br /> Once you've thought up your guess, open up urbandictionary and see how you fared. For bonus points, post whether you've tried it.<br /> <br /> Happy guessing! :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Urban Dictionary is your friend. It will introduce you to all sorts of things you both did, and didnt want to know. In the case of &quot;Paizuri&quot;, I consider it about &quot;MEH&quot; in terms of sensation, but it still remains exciting for other reasons if you let them do it for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/771-starmage21","name":"Starmage21","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T02:00:11-08:00","id":325872,"title":"","content":"I'm not desiring sexual activity so much as craving the casual and personal intimacy that comes with a sexual relationship. I miss holding someone at night, or the simple joy of leaning over and kissing the person you've chosen to be with. I don't mean to sound morose or spiritually deprived in some manner, but I think that's what really hurts me most about being single.<br /> I naturally feel detached from my fellow man. I don't want to feel that way, and I'm not giving up on being social just because I can't seem to get a date. I'm just seriously craving some emotional or physical intimacy, not necessarily sexual in nature (but I'm not opposed to the idea.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T07:05:31-08:00","id":325974,"title":"","content":"I can't say I quite get that desire myself--a craving for distance from people and for personal solitude is pretty deep in my psyche--but it sounds perfectly normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T12:24:40-08:00","id":326207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath