ority and the disturbing minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>We pretty much agree about the law as it is, I think, but can I ask why you think the law should make a difference between the &quot;relative [sic] reasonable majority&quot; and the &quot;disturbing minority&quot;? I realise we all come from different legal systems, but from what I understand of mine, anyone can do anything they want to their own body. If you want to kill yourself, that's not forbidden by law. Others should probably try to stop you, but the law can't. To a lesser extent, you can consent to being subjected to many actions that would otherwise be illegal. To me, it seems like the &quot;disturbing minority&quot; would either be within their rights, in which case I see no reason to suddenly change that, or already overstepping them, no matter this new law.<br /> <br /> I mean, if we were to make it illegal for people to put themselves at risk, then drafting people for the army would no longer be allowed.<br /> <br /> Also, the use of the adjectives &quot;reasonable&quot; and &quot;disturbing&quot; to describe the groups is problematic. Provided it is consensual, the fact that something disturbs us is not grounds to make it illegal. In fact, that's kind of leaning the same way as I feel the UK sex law already is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=341973#post341973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can never find RACK admissible because there's always one party that is stronger and able to manipulate/pressure physically but more importantly psychologically and leads the other party to do things they are not comfortable with but are coerced into. SSC is the only way to keep it normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>If people are into RACK, I don't think they're interested in &quot;keep[ing] it normal&quot;. :P<br /> <br /> Really though, as you say, the risk that one party is psychologically stronger than the other party is always present. This is true for all kinds of sexual relationships and, on a wider note, all relationships in general. Any abusive relationships can lead to great damage, and while a RACK one might lend itself to some more vivid images of just what could happen, I'd hesitate to make it essentially different from others.<br /> <br /> Also, the fact that someone is coercing someone else already makes the &quot;C&quot;s in both initialisms moot. If we are talking coersion, then we're no longer talking either RACK or SSC, we are talking abuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T13:21:30-08:00","id":342170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=342165#post342165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue anima