ng","name":"ndisi the king","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T13:51:28-08:00","id":343193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starmage21</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=343159#post343159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not necessarily convinced that it is higher risk. Nerve damage associated with needles is more than likely going to be an extremely local affair, if it causes a problem at all. Keep in mind that acupuncture is specifically about sticking needles into nerve bundles, and the chinese have been on top of that for what seems like ancient history. While I've seen sports injuries that will never heal, and seen rope suspensions that can paralyze entire limbs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Safe is always a relative concept. Even vanilla sex carries risks. Even lack of sex carries risks.<br /> <br /> IMO the key is education, understanding and evaluation. I don't mind if people do more risky activities... after all they are the ones at risk. I just object to the ignorant experimentation on yourself or others. Do you know the risks of rope suspension and how to mitigate them as much as possible? Then don't do rope suspension until you learn, and then decide if you still want to? Substitute anything you want in that phrase for rope suspension and the answer is the same. Heck the answer is the same with hang gliding, base jumping or crossing the street. Know what the risks are, decide if you want to accept them and/or what can be done to reduce them, and go from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T15:22:54-08:00","id":343333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ndisi the king</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=343190#post343190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never had sex before but it looks like I might finally have a shot at punching the card. the catch? girl is probably fattest person at school. any tips for a brittle first timer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get below her? :P<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, as someone who's only just out the crib in that respect myself, what I did was just to be chill about it. I had the luck of being with someone more experienced than I, and who was thus able to guide my trembling hands, often literally. If this is the case with your partner, I'd advise you to listen with interest and let her teach you, all while communicating. I found that asking questions helped me learn a lot and made it all a bit more playful, like she was actually my teacher. After all, everyone needs to learn the ropes first.<br /> <br /> If you and your partner are equally inexperienced, talk to each other and find out what you both like, or feel like doing, or are interested in. Remember that sex does not equal penetration, and a successful session does not have to contain it. If you're worried about your partner being a big girl, use positions that will not put your strength to test. Prior research is encouraged!<br /> <br /> Expect the first time to be bad. Not trying to get you down, but sex is a skill you learn by doing. It might feel like you're finally finishing but this is actually when you start.<br /> <br /> On a sidenote, the comment about her weight kind of sticks out to me? Now, I get that you want to have sex, and I'm all in favour of casual sex between consenting adults, but that little clause together with some other wording somehow makes me wonder if you really want to have sex <i>with her</i> or if you're just taking who will have you? No matter how casual, sex has an emotional component. Don't do anything you'd be ashamed of in the morning. Of course, I may just be rambling here, but you asked for advice and there it is. :P<br /> <br /> Use condoms, mkay?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 12-17-2014, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T10:32:16-08:00","id":343989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_co