allout can go for ages after. And I don't mean pregnancy or STDs; condoms take care of like 99% of that. No, I'm talking about the emotional and social angle. Sex complicates things, especially the first time.<br /> <br /> Like I said, sex is great, but try to see past that, and think, &quot;is this under the understanding that this is part of a relationship? If so, <i>is</i> it part of the relationship? Or am I just so excited for sex that I'll do/say anything?&quot; Being dishonest, either with your partner or yourself, in these questions <i>will</i> cause lots of problems for you later. And frankly, for your first time (which <i>will</i> suck), it may not be worth the hassle. Maybe better waiting for a time when those questions can be answered honestly. If nothing else, it'll make the days and weeks after a hell of a lot easier. Plus, greater chance of repeat performances. Which is always great.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Huh. Guy's been banned. Oh well, I'll leave this here, someone else may benefit from reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T08:19:10-08:00","id":348342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\