348937,"title":"","content":"Remember that courtly love was just an ideal even in medieval age. Knights did not behave like in chivalric legends. A Raubritter is better representative of medieval age than a knight errant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T10:05:44-08:00","id":349126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=348937#post348937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that courtly love was just an ideal even in medieval age. Knights did not behave like in chivalric legends. A Raubritter is better representative of medieval age than a knight errant.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I understand it, it wasn't much of a thing even then, with most of what we consider stock chivalric treatment being an appendix added much later in the victorian era as people idolized the &quot;simple&quot; &quot;pure&quot; &quot;honorable&quot; age that never really was. <br /> <br /> So my thoughts? If it's a fun pretend thing to do for all parties involved go for it? But ultimately it's a game of sex appeal, not unlike the writing of poetry, doing the Alpha Male tough guy act or any one of a host of other things, and ultimately it does break down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T11:02:11-08:00","id":349168,"title":"","content":"You make valid points that I find difficult to argue against, Kat and Canuck. I had a feeling that this was a flimsy idea, but I'm a sucker for romantic ideals.<br /> I'm likely immature in that way, I suppose. A large part of me just wants to be my 8 year old self's ideal image of what being grown Me up was: The heartfelt guy that travels far and wide if need be, braving danger and loneliness to find that someone that loves me.<br /> <br /> I'm not pointing any fingers....but I BLAME <i>THE PRINCESS BRIDE</i>!!<br /> <br /> I know that there's more at work here in my head than a timeless film filled with propaganda, but that discussion would likely be pointless without some serious therapy first.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy name is Jose Santiago de Polanco. You kill my stupid idea. Prepare to hug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-betwee