self to attempt experiencing brief respites from the pain of the loneliness. I try so hard to give life a chance. I feel unwanted, unworthy and ugly. I likely am.<br /> <br /> The closest thing I have to a hug is curling up under a blanket. The only cuddling I can do is just me squeezing a pillow while I try to rationalize a meaning for me existing. I'm so tired of crying all alone, hungering for a singlescrap of affection from someone who might care. <br /> <br /> I'm pathetic. I'm so lonely that I'll devote hours of my day to daydreaming about people that I know telling me that they love me and being held by them. None of my friends or acquaintances think of me that way, Nobody wants me.<br /> I don't understand. I've never cheated or acted unfaithfully to whomever I'm dating. I try to be understanding and loving.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter, though. No matter how hard I try, what I go through will never win me love. The life I live will be lived alone, with no kindred spirit to smile across the table at me. I'm not what anyone would want. I'm a last resort. I'm emotionally starved benough that being last on someone's list would still flatter me<br /> <br /> Even if they don't love me, I would throw myself away just need to hear a sweet voice say my name with some semblance of desire or affection. I'd give up a kidney just to have a real chance to love. No, I'm saying that wrong. I would give up every single thing in my life just to be loved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","d