ood or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T19:01:25-08:00","id":359811,"title":"","content":"Sign me up to get &quot;robbed&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T22:02:27-08:00","id":359875,"title":"","content":"Azreal:<br /> <br /> I too have had a lack of relationships, and spent a long time emotionally where you are. I'm 27 as well, but have kind of grown out of it. The older I've gotten I've simply devoted more free time into personal development and learning. Learn to meditate, read more books, study up on philosophy. Try to see the world from different points of view. I've come to cherish my independence so much that I even portion out my time to my friends, being very selfish with it. What I do I do for me.<br /> <br /> And I really do get where you're coming from, I mean that, I was a wreck for years, and I -never- -never- talked to anyone about it, I bottled it up and let it simmer on the inside and it really fucked me up. I did have a series of events that kind of &quot;cured&quot; me, but the biggest one was learning to work on me and learning to meditate. I firmly believe that we only get what we're ready for, and you have to work on you before you're ready for a relationship.<br /> <br /> It wasn't until I went through my big &quot;spiritual meditation learning phase,&quot; that I met the perfect girl, and had a lovely relationship for 3 years. That ended too though, in the end it became too codependent, and we smothered each other. From the outside we had the perfect relationship, and everyone was shocked when we quietly ended it after a lengthy discussion about how we lost our own identities to the idea of our relationship.<br /> <br /> Just another lesson I'm happy to have learned. Since then I've turned down two advances for a relationship because I know exactly what I want from a relationship now that would add to what I have. I no longer desire simply to be in a relationship for it's own sake, it has to be the right kind to add to what I already have going on, which is pretty enjoyable constant alone time. It's kind of like Carl Jungs idea of individualism, that through becoming the most ourselves, we eventually will see how best to integrate into our societies.<br /> <br /> So too it is with relationships, by becoming the best you that you can be, you will eventually see what you actually want, not just what you think you want.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, read up on transcendental meditation. Or if you want to low ball it, read Eckhart Tole's &quot;The Power of Now,&quot; and try to absorb the good bits. The biggest change I had in my life was learning to turn off my brain's rampant and constant need to tell me what it though would make me happy. Imagine at minimum being about to at least stop thinking about all this shit without your control. Hey, it worked for me.<br /> <br /> I wish you all the best,<br /> Mark<br /> <br /> PS: I apologize if my message isn't exactly clear or well worded, I was about to go to bed, and saw your posted and felt compelled to at least offer something despite hardly ever ending up in the off topic boards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T01:29:56-08:00","id":360011,"title":"","content":"Thanks Mark!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> All the best and thank you for thinking of me and for putting the time and thought into your encouraging message.<br /> <br /> Now, here's where I tell you that I've done the soul-searching, the reading (I'm the asshole that reads Atlas Shrugged on the toilet.), and that I've TRIED meditation for years, both in guided fashion by trained professionals and by myself. My mind gets bored. Feeling like an empty husk without desire isn't enlightening. It's boring as balls.<br /> I think our ideas of what's romantic have become cerebral to the point of near-parody. We are affected into what amounts to an artificial and accepted false reality. In the cases of other cultural phenomena of that sort, many cultures have the luxury of acknowledging these concepts, such as hikikomori in Japan. My problem is that we don't acknowledge that we're doing a dance. We'll joke about it. We'll even theorize about it.....but we won't accept it.<br /> Did your first kiss feel ever-so-special? Mine came with a cold nose and the taste of chicken tenders.<br /> Was losing your virginity the way you expected it to be? HAHAHAHAHAHA HAHA MY NAME'S NOT BRIAN!<br /> <br /> I also don't think that people who think I'm unhappy really know me. Am I a pessimist? Possibly. A pragmatist. Sure. A gloomy Gus? Not really. I'm loud, opinionated, and my most common noises are giggling and off-key singing.<br /> <br /> I find humor in most of life. I feel fucked up, don't get me wrong, but I have had traumatic experiences and a genetic predisposition to mental illness all my life. I feel fucked up, as well, because I find the world to be fucked up. Now, I could call on my family's entrenched background in the 12 steps and, like the serenity prayer suggests, accept the things I cannot change.<br /> <br /> That kinda sounds like what wusses and cowards do, though, right??<br /> <br /> I'm serious. If a protagonist in a movie came to that conclusion, you'd lose all respect for the motherfucker.<br /> In the words of Cypress Hill, We Ain't Goin Out Like That.<br /> <br /> I think I'd much rather do what I usually do when I'm told I can't or shouldn't do something: Do it anyway, and proceed to have statistically average results. I might bitch and complain a lot, but much of my lack of intimacy is simply due to the fact that most people bother me. Not in a small way. Across the web, on celluloid covered in blood or in animated form, people are alright. You take those filters away and I suddenly feel crowded and annoyed.<br /> <br /> \u200bI like people in very small doses. One of the reasons I think it's great if your partner is your best friend is that it means ONE LESS PERSON! They're covering both jobs. I'm going to fuck things up. I'm going to be alone, and hate it. When I'm not alone, I'll be happier. Can't be happy all the time, and it feels like I'm dabbling in Scientology every time I start to think otherwise.<br /> <br /> I'm going to cry until my face aches and my stomach is in knots.<br /> I'm going to doubt everyone and everything around me.<br /> One day, without a shadow of a doubt, I am going to die.<br /> <br /> The <i>idea</i> of having love makes all of these facts tolerable.<br /> <br /> How many of your dreams and wishes going to come true, kids?<br /> <br /> Doesn't matter. I believe in an ideal I may never reach. If I'm so Damn sure there's something up in the attic for me, why shouldn't I build a ladder to heaven? I might die tomorrow.<br /> <br /> \u200bSelf-improvement is just learning to love yourself in more ways. Last time I checked, that was just called wanking. I want love, but I'd rather earn it through getting my heart broken again and again until I find who I love. than by learning a new jig in the dance and hoping that I'll attract some robotic answer to my insectile new behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 01-06-2015, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T21:18:46-08:00","id":360917,"title":"","content":"Did you guys know orgasm headaches were a thing? Ow, ow, ow, ow .... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T22:56:25-08:00","id":361023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=360917#post360917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you guys know orgasm headaches were a thing? Ow, ow, ow, ow .... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>'holy crap seriously?<br /> <br /> I aalways thought they cured headaches but it does make sense they coudld cause one for some people...our bodies are fucking weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T00:06:42-08:00","id":361054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=360917#post360917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you guys know orgasm headaches were a thing? Ow, ow, ow, ow .... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A friend's sister has situational Moyamoya; it doesn't generally affect her on a day-to-day basis, but when she has orgasms, the artery-constriction to the brain kicks in and she passes out afterwards (usually for only a minute to a few minutes), and can have a headache afterwards. (Still worth it, though, she says...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T08:25:23-08:00","id":361315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=360917#post360917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you guys know orgasm headaches were a thing? Ow, ow, ow, ow .... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! About a year ago I found out exactly how bad they could be. I have a healthy sexual appetite that my wife couldnt possibly keep up with, even though she tries. The first time I got hit with the headache was after sex and it just hurt a bit. Apparently, that is your signal to lay off for a bit, and I didnt, and they got progressively worse. It got to the point where i'd taken 1000mg of ibuprofen ahead of time just to deal with the impending pain, and it was quite bad.<br /> After day 6 or 7, I decided to say &quot;fuck it&quot; and just stopped all forms of sexual activity for the week or so it takes for all that to reset. 2 days into it I fell off the wagon and masturbated, totally thinking that I might be able to get away with it and I was dead wrong. I came quickly and the headache hit me so hard that I was dizzy and nearly fell out of my chair. It was some of the worst pain i have ever felt, and it lasted a good 5 minutes before dulling to a manageable level. It was everything I needed to take the next 7 days off.<br /> I'm STILL afraid they'll come back. The last one hurt just THAT bad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/771-starmage21","name":"Starmage21","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T09:35:12-08:00","id":361388,"title":"","content":"I've also had a brief encounter with such headaches. Or such a headache, rather, because it only happened once.<br /> <br /> It was at some point in my teens, maybe I was somewhere between 17 or 19? The cause was an intense bout of masturbation, we're talking possibly ten consecutive rapid-fire climaxes. Towards the end, I wasn't even getting erections anymore, but I still didn't want to stop. Well, I finally did stop when the last orgasm caused me to cry out in pain and slump against a chair. If felt like someone had shot an arrow straight through my ears, an intense, stinging pain that lasted a good minute before it waned. I took the damn hint, that's for sure, and I kept off it for a couple days. Luckily, it hasn't returned since then, and I'm happy if it never does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T09:55:29-08:00","id":361405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https:/