alled out as requiring &quot;proof&quot;, if you will, or is the general understanding of the bisexual condition more nuanced than I give people credit for?<br /> <br /> If you do in fact not identify as bisexual, I will take one of those strikes to the spine so kindly demonstrated by Azrael above and scurry off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 02-25-2015, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:45:34-08:00","id":419539,"title":"","content":"I'm obiously neither Azrael, nor Ceocoyotl, but as I'm also bisexual maybe I can also share my experiences <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />?<br /> <br /> Yeah, in my experience people tend to asume you are either straight or gay depending on the percieved gender of your current partner, after all there are not many people going out with both a guy and a girl at the same time, always, so people get the idea, right?<br /> <br /> Some even go so far as to say they <i>don't believe</i> in bisexuality, like they tell you to your face there's no such things as, well, <i>you</i>. I supose I don't have to say how utterly offensive that is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: but far worse are those that believe you and just find you horrible, I've been called everything from <i>mutant</i> (no kidding!) to the most common <i>degenerate</i>, <i>pervert</i> and other less typeable epithets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-25-2015, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:38:42-08:00","id":419617,"title":"","content":"To clarify, yes I am bisexual. I have been since I was 13. For people trying to grasp bisexuals they usually or sometimes misunderstand us. I can see why many would be confuse on the matter since we usually pick the opposite gender or the same, not sure which to &quot;label&quot; us, correct? I, myself, am attracted to both because I see both genders as beautiful. I find being bisexual to be a blissful freedom to look both ways in what humanity has to offer. Bisexuality I also see it as a path for beginners who are searching for themselves and their sexuality. Again I have already accepted what I am a long time ago, and I love it. I find being with a women to be magnificent and the same for a man, whether we have different genitals or the same. And yes, I do understand that at one point I will have to settle for one gender if I ever get married in the future. If I settle with a man I will still feel attractive towards women and I will still consider myself as bisexual because that's what I am and that's what I feel. <br /> <br /> If your curious to know more about bisexuality, then look at the LGBT thread. There are amazing people in there to talk to and to learn from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"att