hat you mean. I had those conversations where bisexuality does not exist because that person is simply confuse. And the sad part is that it also comes from the gay community as well. I had this one gay guy try to prove me wrong on my sexuality until later on I found out he was trying to convert me into becoming fully gay with him. I scoffed at him and flipped him off. I say bullshit, we are here and we do exist! I love both men and women. <br /> <br /> Oh sorry dude. That totally sucks. Ever since I came out ignorant people (mainly Christians, no offense to anyone) have called me pervert and lost soul. I laughed at them and told them they were nothing but hypocrites. As for pervert I took that name with great pride after I try to seduce one of the chicks to get into her pants. Of course she didn't give in but her face was blushing red lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T02:11:19-08:00","id":422723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=419647#post419647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say bullshit, we are here and we do exist! I love both men and women.</div> </div> </div> </div>*fist in the air* Represented!<br /> <br /> Anyhoo...<br /> <br /> <br /> I have a strange mental stew on the brain-stove tonight, but the part that's relevant to the thread is this:<br /> <br /> I forgot how much of my (very dusty. Only slightly used, though.) sex life centered around BDSM. Looking back, I've literally never been in any romantic relationship that didn't include a fair amount of bondage, Sado-masochism or Dominance and Submission play. It was, weirdly, hardly ever discussed. It was just how things went. Huh.<br /> <br /> The thing about it is, I forgot the extent of the play because I find a lot of genuine emotional sincerity in my BDSM play and in people who live the lifestyle. I had just mentally filed all that as Intimacy, without further descriptors. I suppose it's because I find that there's an honesty in wanting to be needed to the point of being willing to be someone's dog or their footstool. Likewise, there's a brutal honesty in wanting to control the behavior and experiences of others.<br /> <br /> A non-sexual example of enjoying that is simply running a game. As a GM/ST, you can do everything and anything, from generating gods and monsters to changing the weather and cracking planets in half, but there's a consensual element to everything on the part of the players, and should be mutually satisfying to both parties.bI miss having more of that honesty, on an intimate level.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to specify that I miss it in my personal life in case someone just assumes that I have a raging Power Boner while I'm Storytelling. No worries. I'm kinky, but I'm not the bastard son of HedonismBot, dipping my bottom in a series of exotic oils while nude servants throw maraschino cherries at my nipples mid-session. That could stain my dice bag!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us ar