com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:29:13-07:00","id":436552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/49646-let-s-talk-about-sex-again?p=430601#post430601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know... My bisexuality preference changes when I'm sleeping with someone or dating someone. I don't know, that's how I see my interest peak up for a gender.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Same. Here.<br /> <br /> If I'm involved with a man, I'll likely be more attracted to masculinity or my partner's general type than women. If I'm dating a woman, I might tend to check out the female form a bit more, on the same token. Sometimes people will insist that if you're bisexual, you must be &quot;missing&quot; the gender that you're not currently dating. In my case, I call bullshit on that.<br /> <br /> For me, sex is a gateway to my real goal:love. I can enjoy sex, for all of its physical pleasure, as well as its intimacy. Hell, you give me the green light, things might get rough....in a good way. I'm a Dom at heart, but I can be a lovely switch in the right situation. I've never been a complete submissive.<br /> Honestly, I kinda envy the courage it takes to commit unconditionally to the dominance of another. To me, that's the sexual equivalent of not flinching with a cocked and loaded gun in your face.<br /> <br /> BDSM