ou've said for any kind of frame of reference at all.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to comment on anything else you said, because I want to avoid any further misconceptions on my part or anyone elses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/771-starmage21","name":"Starmage21","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T21:23:46-07:00","id":667769,"title":"","content":"For my part, SM21, I consider any mental anguish I suffered due to intense and merciless introspection an early payment for the foolishness and broken goddamn intentions that I let into the world.. <br /> <br /> If you hadn't guessed, I was drunk enough that my blood was almost flammable when I made the epic decision to help a woman cheat on her husband the other night. I should clarify the evil deed, though. Not detail. Clarify.<br /> <br /> Apparently I use the word &quot;hump&quot; pretty fucking liberally when I'm smashed. You humped, Humpday. I just saw boobs on Skype from another hemisphere because someone who calls me their friend has decided that she hates her marriage and husband, but refuses to leave. She instead has chosen to basically have &quot;secret boyfriends&quot; on the internet. I'm quoting that, not because she's used those words ,but because it sounds less awful than the far more creepy &quot;fiance&quot;. <br /> <br /> Yeah, she's married and still seeks a &quot;fiance&quot;. I don't even know what to make of that, so I'll leave that there. <br /> <br /> So, being the pathetically lonely douchebag I am, I let her convince me that I should be &quot;hers&quot;. She does things I like and says she loves me to rebel against a marriage she hates. A marriage she hates becau